---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { terminalQuotes } from '../data/quotes';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const creed = terminalQuotes.slice(0, 4);
---

<Layout title="About">
	<section class="section">
		<div class="wrap narrow">
			<p class="eyebrow">// history</p>
			<h1>About Senescent Gaming</h1>

			<p>
				Senescent Gaming traces back to LAN nights running over IPX/SPX,
				matchmaking through Kali, and browsing servers on GameSpy 3D — an era
				when finding a game took longer than playing one. It was never just
				one genre: shooters for the reflexes, RTS for the spreadsheets
				disguised as strategy, and eventually MOBAs once someone discovered
				you could argue about lane assignments for longer than the match
				itself. What started as a loose group of regulars who kept showing up
				to the same servers turned into something closer to a team, mostly
				because nobody else wanted to put up with our callouts. A couple of
				us even ran Counter-Strike through CAL's amateur ladder back when
				"going pro" meant a free mousepad — a run best remembered for its
				jerseys and its losses, in roughly that order.
			</p>

			<p>
				The name is the joke and the point. <em>Senescent</em> means aging —
				and while the current esports scene loves crowning teenagers as
				"veterans" after two seasons, we've been doing this since before most
				pro rosters' players were born. We don't have faster reflexes than we
				used to. We have better positioning, worse knees, and absolutely no
				patience for being spammed with "hey want to join our clan" messages.
			</p>

			<h2>What we actually do</h2>
			<p>
				Play the games we've always played, on our own schedule, with people
				we already trust. We are not actively recruiting, scouting, or
				accepting tryouts — see the <a href={`${base}join`}>recruitment page</a> for
				the long version of that short answer.
			</p>

			<h2>The name, if you're still wondering</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>Senescent</strong> (adj.): growing old. That's it. That's the
				bit.
			</p>

			<h2>Words we sort of live by</h2>
			<ul class="creed">
				{creed.map((line) => <li class="mono">{line}</li>)}
			</ul>

			<h2>System requirements to join our scrims</h2>
			<div class="sysreq">
				<h3>Minimum</h3>
				<dl>
					<dt>CPU</dt>
					<dd>Pentium 133MHz or a working knee, whichever you still have</dd>
					<dt>RAM</dt>
					<dd>32MB, plus whatever you can still remember from 1999</dd>
					<dt>Storage</dt>
					<dd>2x CD-ROM drive, or a bag of old jewel cases for nostalgia</dd>
					<dt>Connection</dt>
					<dd>A modem and low expectations</dd>
				</dl>
				<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Recommended</h3>
				<dl>
					<dt>CPU</dt>
					<dd>Pentium II 300MHz or better lumbar support</dd>
					<dt>GPU</dt>
					<dd>3dfx Voodoo2, or reading glasses with anti-glare coating</dd>
					<dt>Connection</dt>
					<dd>A phone line nobody else in the house needs right now</dd>
					<dt>Other</dt>
					<dd>Unlimited patience and a heating pad within arm's reach</dd>
				</dl>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.narrow {
		max-width: 70ch;
	}

	.narrow p {
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.narrow h2 {
		color: var(--fg);
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}

	.narrow em,
	.narrow strong {
		color: var(--fg);
	}

	.creed {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.creed li {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-left: 2px solid var(--accent-dim);
		background: var(--bg-card);
		border-radius: 2px;
	}
</style>
